	)
	(text "PLACEMENT (the SBC and the modules are on opposite sides of the board)\n  J1, J2: BBB headers, 2x23 male pins, bodies on the BOTTOM side, long pins down into the BBB sockets. Pin 1 of P8/P9 as on the BBB.\n  J4..J12, jumpers, test points, ferrites, caps: TOP side. Keep ~25 mm clear above the BBB Ethernet/USB/HDMI area.\n  Put the analog front end (R33, R34, C1, D1, D2, R38) next to J8 and P9.34/P9.39. One star point for GND/AGND (R38).\nSIGNALS\n  SYN_CLK/SYN_DATA/SYN_LE: SPI0 mode 0, MSB first, 32-bit words. SYN_LD is an input to the SBC. SYN_CE and SYN_PDR are static.\n  ATT_V1..V6 = 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 dB (assumed, high = stage in). Verify with tools/bringup.py pe4302-walk.\n  BBB I2C2 (P9.19/20) drives I2C_SCL/I2C_SDA for the ADS1115.\nOPEN POINTS: PE4302 and ADF4351 header pin order, detector OUT pin, DC jack polarity, ferrite and fuse values: confirm with a DMM.\nUnused BBB pins carry no connection (X). Names of unused BBB pins come from the BBB system reference, not from the repo."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17 437 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.15 1.15)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f3ad7044-38cb-5a5a-9785-c667fc5e247b")
	)
	(text "Ferrite beads isolate the module supplies from the SBC rails."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 442 115 0)
		(effects
